        <headline>High Wind Warning issued September 26 at 1:24PM EDT until September 27 at 8:00AM EDT by NWS Boston/Norton MA</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...Northeast winds 20 to 30 mph with gusts of 45 to 60 mph.

* WHERE...The eastern Massachusetts coast as well as the south coasts
of both Rhode Island and Massachusetts. This includes Cape Cod and
the Islands.

* WHEN...Until 8 AM EDT Sunday.

* IMPACTS...Damaging winds will blow down trees and power lines.
Power outages are expected. Travel will be difficult, especially
for high profile vehicles.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...The long duration of the winds coupled with
heavy rain and fully leafed trees may exacerbate the risk for tree
damage and power outages.
</description>
        <instruction>People are urged to secure loose objects that could be blown around
or damaged by the wind.</instruction>
